Subject: [PATCH] Guard against invalid/missing VigiEau data and tell the user

Transparency note: this patch was written by an AI (Claude, Anthropic) at the request of
the user (Eric Rodi, BerrySwann on GitHub), who asked me to say so openly. It is a
proposal, written against 0.12.7 and not run against a live Home Assistant instance
(Python syntax check only). Please review it critically before merging.

Behaviour:
- when the coordinator update fails, or data is None / malformed / has an unknown level,
  AlertLevelEntity logs one warning (not one per poll) and sets a data_available=false
  attribute plus the reason;
- the numeric sensor falls back to 0; the text sensor keeps its last state;
- a persistent notification says VigiEau data is unavailable (and that 0 does not mean
  no restriction); it is dismissed automatically when data is back.

---
